# Cloudflare API credentials for certbot-dns-cloudflare.
#
# Copy this file to `cloudflare.ini`, replace the placeholder with a real API
# token, and restrict its permissions:
#
#   cp cloudflare.ini.example cloudflare.ini
#   chmod 600 cloudflare.ini
#
# `cloudflare.ini` is gitignored. Never commit a real token.
#
# An API token is preferred over the legacy global API key: it can be scoped to
# the single zone this certificate needs. Certbot 5.6.0's plugin also accepts
# `dns_cloudflare_email` + `dns_cloudflare_api_key`, but that key grants full
# access to the whole Cloudflare account.
dns_cloudflare_api_token = replace-with-cloudflare-api-token
